      "title": "Stepwise pressure reduction recovers heat",
      "description": "Hot digested slurry is let down in steps to lower pressures; in each tank part of the water flashes to steam and the slurry cools to the saturation temperature of that stage. The flash vapour from each stage heats incoming slurry in the matching heater stage (regenerative heating). Erosion at let-down valves and inlets is a key concern.",
